                <pb facs="0777" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4A6/373: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-04T14:00:00+01:00">July 4, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 4—9:43 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>37. My telegram No. 34, July 2, 10 a.m. Article 23 of draft convention withdrawn.
                    Swiss amendment adopted this morning without objection with the phrase “in
                    accordance with the constitutional procedure of each of the parties to the
                    dispute” in the second paragraph deleted. Certain drafting changes summed up by
                    the legal adviser of the Secretariat will be made. This delegation stated that
                    it reserved its position on this subject until the second reading.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
